  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A simple pendulum oscillates with period <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span> on Earth. The mass of the pendulum is doubled and oscillates on the Moon where the acceleration due to gravity is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{6}\"></span> that of Earth. The length of the pendulum stays the same.</p>\n<p>What is the period of the pendulum on the Moon?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{12}T\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{6}T\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{3}T\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{2}T\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
